WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions for the partner / affiliate guided tour, recorded on a phone on
2026-09-21 (65.2s).

NOTE
The recording has NO audio. That is measured, not assumed: the file carries an
AAC track, but it is digital silence — mean and max volume both -91 dB across
all 5,746,560 samples. So there is nothing to transcribe and these captions
carry the whole thing.

NOTE
The seven step titles and their wording are taken from tourSteps() in
index.html, not transcribed from the screen, so they match the product exactly.
If the tour copy changes, re-derive this file from the source rather than
editing it by hand.

NOTE
Timings come from scene-cut detection on the recording. Every step boundary
except one lands on a measured cut, because each step switches tab. The
exception is step 1 to step 2, which stays on the Partners tab and only swaps
the dialog text — too small a change to register — so that boundary was pinned
by reading the step counter at 0.8s intervals: "1 of 7" at 13.6s, "2 of 7" at
14.4s. The tail timings after 35s are accurate to about a second where no cut
exists.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
This recording has no sound. The captions carry it.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.100
A new Lite account — facility and staff compliance only. No MAR, no 602A, no PHI.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:10.600
Walkthrough offers both: take the tour on screen, or read the same seven screens.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.000
Step 1 of 7 — Your trainers and their codes. One row per trainer: their link, how many signed up through it, how many of those are paying, and the commission rate on record.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Step 2 — A code is a longer trial. Somebody arriving on a trainer's link gets the trial length set on that code instead of the default.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.150
Step 3 — This is the number that matters. Requirements that are current, out of requirements that exist. Here, 7 of 119.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:23.120
Step 4 — And it tells you whose. Six overdue, 55 due this month. An expired TB test is a named person, not a red number on a chart.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.650
Step 5 — The checklist an analyst works from. Title 22 requirements with dates against them, overdue at the top.

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:30.050
Step 6 — Now ask me something. Tello answers from this facility's own records.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:35.050
Step 7 — Everything else is in here. Documents, the audit log, billing. Walkthrough replays this tour any time.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:41.950
Back on the dashboard: overdue items with their dates, then the quick actions.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:50.190
The menu — staff, in-service, training, lessons, team access, checklist, documents, Tello, audit log, billing, partners.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:57.000
Documents. Upload a file, tag what it is, and it is stored privately.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:05.200
Billing — the current plan, then Lite at $29, Multi-Home at $79, and Agency as Contact Sales.
